                        "language": "english",
                        "review": ".... where do i begin....\n\nI can see the idea where they thought this would been a great game but some where down the line someone messed up baddly... \n\nfirst of all good idea to simulate the characters.... first game that did it u get a 10 for that.... but then.... i looked at how we explore....\n\nunderstand some where down the line you dont just let your man wonder into a zombie infested world then he just begin to take damage... what happened to making decisions? how did he get hurt why did he go there.... text rpg can be just a fun if done right..... \n\nI feel as though this game was rushed.... here is my comment for the dev take this game and do more work its too bare bone  nice visual on the characters who are generated but... the game play.... the whole  thing feels so under whelming.... after 5 mins of playing i put this game down.\n\nfocus on how your team utilize the equipment in the scenario's, how it effect their chances in an encounter, focus on making the character make decisions..\n\nthis is just the minor  its text based you don't have to focus too hard on the models from what i seen in combat make sure the items literally are effective if a barricade is put up let it hold .....\n\n.... as it stands this game is still in need of a lot of work.... i didn't see too many glitches given it didn't hold my interest long enough for me to investigate that...\n\nAll im going to say is this... you started on the right track focus on bettering the game where it becomes interesting im not gonna say great game but i will say keep working on it.\n\nYou can do it get more fresh ideas and add them here also give your self more time to make the game better dont rush it if its not ready its not ready...\n",
